  {
    "id": "99809d60-d4ff-4e3e-a457-624189bfa764",
    "title": "1. TPU resume bug \u2014 trainer_pytorch.py, end of load_checkpoint (~line 346):\n      if getattr(self, \"use_master_weights\", False):\n          for p, mp in self.param_to_master:\n              mp.data.copy_(p.data.float())\n      Without this, resuming a TPU run overwrites loaded weights with stale init values on the first optimizer step.\n\n      2. MLX memory limit semantics \u2014 trainer_mlx.py:111-116: the tier budget should go to mx.metal.set_wired_limit (resident-memory control), not set_memory_limit (an evaluation guideline that throws exceptions when exceeded). Log failures instead of bare except: pass \u2014 the wired limit errors if it exceeds the system limit (sudo sysctl iogpu.wired_limit_mb=\u2026 to raise it).\n\n      3. SPMD benchmark double-count \u2014 trainer_pytorch.py:405-406: gate world_mult on not self.is_spmd \u2014 in SPMD mode bs is already the global batch, so tokens/sec is inflated \u00d7N cores.\n\n      4. Optional hygiene: delete or wire the dead tpu:/mac:/gpu:/lightning: blocks in configs/unified/*.yaml (read by nothing), set compile: true in a CUDA config if you want torch.compile active, and move scratch/test_mlx_compile_lr.py + the master-weights test into tests/ as regression tests.\n\nPlease ensure these bugs have been fixed.",
